{
  // Typechecking for the guard and verification scripts in `scripts/`.
  //
  // ── Why this exists ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // `tsconfig.json` includes only `src/**/*`, so nothing ever typechecked
  // `scripts/`. Most of those scripts are also run with `ts-node -T`
  // (transpile-only), which skips typechecking at run time too. The result is
  // that a script could be wrong in a way TypeScript knows about and nobody
  // would hear until someone ran it.
  //
  // The failure mode this actually produced, three separate times, is
  // constructor arity drift: a service gains a dependency, every call site in
  // `src` is updated because tsc demands it, and the script that constructs
  // the same class by hand is not, because nothing checks it.
  //
  //   • verify-device-rpc.ts    built CoAPAdapter with 7 of 8 arguments
  //                             → `this.deviceAuth` undefined, 5 checks died
  //   • verify-permissions.ts   built PermissionGuard with 3 of 4
  //                             → every "is allowed" check failed AND every
  //                               "is denied" check passed for the wrong
  //                               reason. The suite reported 12 passes while
  //                               testing nothing.
  //   • verify-telemetry-retention.ts  built TelemetryService with 8 of 9
  //
  // The second one is why this config is worth having: a guard that fails is
  // noisy and gets fixed, but a guard that passes vacuously is worse than no
  // guard, because it is counted as evidence.
  //
  //   npm run typecheck:scripts
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "declaration": false,
    // Scripts legitimately reach into private-ish internals and construct
    // services by hand with `as any` stubs. The point of this config is to
    // catch arity and signature drift, not to hold scripts to the build's
    // declaration-emit rules.
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["scripts/**/*.ts", "src/**/*"],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "src/test",
    "src/**/__tests__/**",
    "src/**/*.spec.ts",
    "src/**/*.test.ts"
  ]
}
